# Files in the deployed directory that must NOT be served as part of the site.
#
# Cloudflare clones the mirror repository and treats the whole checkout as the
# asset directory, so without this it uploads the repository's own plumbing.
# The first deploy attempt read 1830 files and was uploading `.git/config`,
# `.git/logs/**` and the sample hooks — publishing the repository's internals
# at the site's own domain. The mirror is a public repo so nothing there is
# secret, but a live `.git` directory on a business website is the kind of
# thing a scanner flags within the hour, and it is a third of the upload for
# nothing.
#
# gitignore-style patterns, read by Wrangler from the root of the asset
# directory at deploy time.

.git
.git/**
.gitignore
.assetsignore

# Wrangler's own scratch and the config file it generates in CI.
.wrangler
.wrangler/**
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml

# The note explaining the mirror to anyone who lands on the repo. It is for
# readers of the repository, not visitors to the site.
README.md

# GitHub Pages marker written by the deploy workflow; meaningless here.
.nojekyll
